*
!.gitignore
!config.toml
!intent.md
!readiness.json
# The two research documents the whole of spec 010 is measured against. They were ignored
# with everything else here, so `docs/requirements.toml` — 411 rows, one per requirement,
# each naming the command that decides it — was the only in-tree record of what they asked
# and nobody but the machine that wrote it could check the copy. A ledger whose source is
# unavailable to its readers is a ledger they have to take on trust, which is the one thing
# this repository refuses everywhere else.
#
# `.ai/` stays disposable and this is the exception that proves it: these two are inputs the
# work is judged against, not state the work produces.
# A shape, not a list. Five lines named two directories and two files one by one, so every
# report after those two was ignored by default and lived only on the machine that made it —
# three of them did, and two of those three could only be ordered by a file date that a
# `git checkout` rewrites. A rule anybody can read from the name is the cure: three digits,
# a hyphen, a name, `.html`, directly in `reports/`. Tested against a real repository: it
# keeps `001-….html` and `010-x.html`, and ignores `notes.html`, `scratch.txt`,
# `0001-four.html` and any loose directory.
!reports/
!reports/[0-9][0-9][0-9]-*.html
